//
// GEMMA4-E2B Q4NX profiling: build the prefill ELFs, run the prefill at CTX and
// capture the result into gemma4_e2b_q4nx.perf.json via bench/extract_perf.py
// (collected by the nightly LLM benchmark). Weights come from the model.q4nx
// bundle pre-seeded into the runner's HF cache.
//
// TTFT ONLY, and that is the difference from the sibling profile tests. Theirs
// measures TTFT *and* decode tok/s over N generated tokens, so extract_perf.py
// records decode_tokens_per_sec as null here.
//
// NOT because the driver is missing -- gemma4_e2b_q4nx_inference.py exists and
// `make profile` measures both halves, which is why this test deliberately runs
// `profile-prefill` instead. It was #1984: the full-depth 35-wave decode
// dispatch hung on this runner, which also put every point of
// run_npu2_sweep.lit in --expect-fail. That hang is fixed (#2008), and the
// sweep now expects failure only at 65536 and 131072 -- an unrelated limit on
// how much host memory XRT will pin for the KV BO, not this defect. Pointing
// this RUN line back at `profile`, passing --n-tokens 64 to extract_perf.py and
// adding a CHECK on a parsed decode_tokens_per_sec is the remaining step,
// deliberately left to its own change so a nightly regression in it is
// attributable.
//
// The nightly derives its per-model row from <model>.perf.json, and for a model
// that ran verify but produced no perf.json it synthesizes an all-null row whose
// documented meaning is "this model's profile compile/run failed". Gemma4's
// prefill does not fail -- so without this test the dashboard would report a
// working engine as a broken one. A real TTFT and a null tok/s says what is
// actually true.
//
// Builds compile-prefill, not compile: no decode template is needed for a TTFT
// measurement, and building one would pull in that 35-wave dispatch.
//
// Perf is best-effort; this test gates only that profiling ran end to end.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, peano_ge22, hfweights_fastflowlm_gemma4_e2b_it_npu2
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_profile
// RUN: cd test_npu2_profile
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile compile-prefill PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile profile-prefill PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | tee profile.txt
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../bench/extract_perf.py profile.txt --model gemma4_e2b_q4nx --n-tokens 0 > gemma4_e2b_q4nx.perf.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < gemma4_e2b_q4nx.perf.json
// CHECK: "model": "gemma4_e2b_q4nx"
// A parsed TTFT, not just a well-formed file: the whole point of this test is
// that the row carries a real number, so if the driver's TTFT line ever drifts
// out of extract_perf.py's regex this must go red rather than publish the null
// row it exists to prevent.
// CHECK: "ttft_ms": {{[0-9]}}
